   112	## 2. Row `(6,4)`, nodal residual class
   113	
   114	Here `a=2`, and contact six is a multiple of `a` strictly below the first
   115	characteristic numerator.  The complete delta-sequence census is
   116	`Delta=(6,4,c)`.  Its gcd chain is `6,2,1`; hence `c` is odd,
   117	`2c in <6,4>`, and `c<12`.  Thus
   118	
   119	| `c` | `beta_1=18-c` | `delta_inf` | `delta_aff` | infinity cluster | `M_inf` |
   120	|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|
   121	| 11 | 7  | 3 | 7 | `(2^3,1,1)` | 8 |
   122	| 9  | 9  | 4 | 6 | `(2^4,1,1)` | 10 |
   123	| 7  | 11 | 5 | 5 | `(2^5,1,1)` | 12 |
   124	| 5  | 13 | 6 | 4 | `(2^6,1,1)` | 14 |
   125	| 3  | 15 | 7 | 3 | `(2^7,1,1)` | 16 |
   126	
   127	This also checks the genus total `10` and every cluster sum directly.  Since
   128	`3d-3=15`, promoted (M-INF) kills the first four nodal configurations.  The
   129	sole numerical threat is `Delta=(6,4,3)`, `beta_1=15`, with three required
   130	nodes.  This is precisely the type for which the reviewed report retracted
   131	the old semigroup argument: its banked witness has an ordinary triple point
   132	and is out of class
   133	(`xmodel/m-inf-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.md:134-168,188-199`).
   134	
   135	The infinity type nevertheless **is attained in the nodal class**.  Put
   136	
   137	```text
   138	r=t^3+t+1,
   139	q=t^4+(2/3)t^2+(4/3)t,
   140	p=r^2.
   141	```
   142	
   143	The exact identity
   144	
   145	```text
   146	8r/27 = p^2-q^3-2pq+(2/3)q^2-(16/27)p+(1/9)q-1/9
   147	```
   148	
   149	gives `C[p,q]=C[r,q]`; since `gcd(deg r,deg q)=1`, its fraction field is
   150	`C(t)`.  The reduced off-diagonal double-point scheme is especially small.
   151	For `sigma=t+s`, `pi=ts`, divided differences of `r` and `q` give
   152	
   153	```text
   154	I_DP=(pi-sigma^2-1, 3sigma^3+4sigma-4).
   155	```
   156	
   157	The cubic has nonzero discriminant.  Its three roots give pair discriminant
   158	`-3sigma^2-4`, which cannot vanish on the cubic, and their common images have
   159	`r=-sigma^3/4=(sigma-1)/3`, `q=(sigma^2+1)/3`, so they are distinct.  Also `r'=0`
   160	forces `q'=4/3`, and the two tangent directions at each pair are distinct
   161	(their determinant has nonzero factors `9sigma^2+4` and
   162	`3sigma^2+4`).  Hence the affine curve has exactly three ordinary nodes and
   163	no diagonal or triple fibre.  Consequently `delta_aff=3` and its degree
   164	semigroup, which contains `<3,4>`, is exactly `<3,4>`.  The sextic genus then
   165	forces `delta_inf=7`; with multiplicity two this is `beta_1=15`.  Thus the
   166	banked triple point is a special member, not a forced feature of the
   167	parametrization structure.
   168	
   169	The remaining structural tests do not kill this witness type.  Its reduced
   170	shape is `(3,2)`, and the scale inequality only requires
   171	`gcd(deg P,deg Q)>=4`.  For the generic slice, either
   172	`(c(Pi),g_L)=(4,0)` or `(2,1)`.  Here `(g;d',n')=(2;3,2)`, so A'(1)--(4)
   173	give one `P`-conjugacy orbit of block products and `P^2` central in
   174	`<U_1,P>`; the equal-product clause does not apply because `4` does not
   175	divide `6` (`xmodel/pi1s4-close-residual-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.md:53-74`).
   176	At the three nodes the abstract assignments
   177	`{(12),(34)}`, `{(13),(24)}`, `{(14),(23)}` show that the pointwise
   178	disjoint-transposition conditions themselves are compatible with generators
   179	of `S_4`.  This is only a local negative control: no promoted result routes
   180	those labels to an infinity-fixed tuple.
   181	
   182	**Verdict: OPEN[PI1S4-(6,4)-FIXED-TUPLE].**  Exactly the nodal
   183	`(beta_1,delta_inf,delta_aff,M_inf)=(15,7,3,16)` configuration survives and
