   471	| nodal `(9,6)` | **OPEN** | Two numerical types `(23;22,6;25)` and `(25;24,4;27)`; nodal realization/exclusion and fixed tuple both missing. |
   472	
   473	The two degree-six tangential kills are unconditional and do not consume
   474	(M-INF-T).  All nodal M-INF kills consume the corrected cluster identity and
   475	the reviewed Nori implication at their stated scopes.  The surviving
   476	numerical rows do not consume a converse from AM admissibility, an attainment
   477	claim, A'(5), or the coprime order fork.  The only in-class attainments proved
   478	here are the target-equivalent three-node survivors in rows `(6,4)` and
   479	`(8,4)`; neither is asserted to carry the global residual `S_4`
   480	representation.
   481	
   482	Accordingly the sweep closes four of the eight charged rows.  The remaining
   483	topological core is one target-isomorphism class of an explicitly nodal
   484	three-node curve, plus six higher-degree AM-numerical types whose nodal
   485	attainment is itself unresolved.  A safe next lemma must be either a
   486	noncoprime braid fixed-tuple theorem with explicit route-to-node data, or an
   487	exact divided-difference realization obstruction for the six numerical
   488	types.  The promoted sources expressly leave the general noncoprime and
   489	residual-double-point problems open
