codex
The fold argument is salvageable, but it omits one necessary descent step: the source-line meridian maps to the square of the target-line meridian before the map factors through the complement of the two lifted curves. The triple-cover sketch has a more serious problem: freeness of a rank-three algebra does not make it globally monogenic. I’m checking that point against a primary triple-cover source and will record the streamed hash; no source file will be saved.
