+Conjugation by `Pi` interchanges `Pi_1` and `Pi_2`, so the outer fixedness and
+braid relation hold. For `(k_1,k_2,k_3)=(0,-5,0)`, the order-three pair action
+gives `S_2=sigma^-5((13),(34))=((14),(13))`. Conjugating by `w'` gives
